# Auto-push to GitHub

The user works on multiple machines and does not want to copy project folders by hand.

- After any `git commit` that the user requested (or that was explicitly allowed), **immediately `git push -u origin HEAD`** (or `git push` if upstream is set).
- Remote: `origin` → `https://github.com/zillawillysu-a11y/CuePlayer_didido.git`
- Do not force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly asks.
- If push fails (auth/network), tell the user clearly and leave the commit local.
- Prefer committing + pushing meaningful slices when the user asks to save/sync work across machines.
